@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Counterfactual Regret Minimization — Equilibrium by Self-Play
' Paper: Regret Minimization in Games with Incomplete Information
' URL:   https://papers.nips.cc/paper_files/paper/2007/hash/08d98638c6fcd194a4b1e6992063e944-Abstract.html
' Level: 1

database  "Information sets\nwhat a player cannot distinguish" as INFO <<db>>
component "Current strategy profile\nprobability per action" as STRAT <<app>>
component "Counterfactual value\nreach-weighted: opponent + chance reach,\nown reach factored out" as CFV <<app>>
component "Regret per action\nwhat not playing it cost" as REG <<async>>
component "Regret matching\nnext strategy from positive regret" as RM <<host>>
database  "Average strategy\napproaches equilibrium" as AVG <<db>>

INFO ARROW_MAIN STRAT : one policy per infoset
STRAT ARROW_MAIN CFV : traverse via self-play
CFV ARROW_MAIN REG : accumulate per action
REG ARROW_QUEUE RM
RM ARROW_MAIN STRAT : next iteration
STRAT ARROW_MAIN AVG : it is the //average//, not the last,\nthat converges

note bottom of REG
  **Decompose regret per information set.** The
  insight is that minimizing regret locally at each
  infoset bounds overall regret, which makes an
  otherwise intractable equilibrium computation
  decomposable and iterative.
  ----
  **The convergence guarantee is narrower than it
  looks.** Average strategies converge to a Nash
  equilibrium in **two-player zero-sum** games. Outside
  that class — more players, or general-sum — CFR
  still minimizes regret, but its average is not a
  Nash equilibrium and carries no such guarantee.
  ----
  **Two things practitioners get wrong.** The
  converging object is the //average// strategy over
  iterations, not the current one; and a mixed
  (randomized) strategy is not a hedge — it is the
  solution, because a deterministic policy in a
  hidden-information game is exploitable.
  ----
  Tabular CFR needs an abstraction to fit real state
  spaces; scaling it with learned values is the ReBeL
  line — Brown, Bakhtin, Lerer & Gong,
  ""arXiv:2007.13544"".
end note
@enduml
